---
title: Beef chili
servings: 8
yield: About 3 quarts, 8 to 10 servings
tags: [american, beef, one-pot, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 2 hours 45 minutes
source: Simple Beef Chili with Kidney Beans by America's Test Kitchen, https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/34-simple-beef-chili-with-kidney-beans
---

Heat the @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a heavy #Dutch oven{} over medium heat until
shimmering.

Add the @yellow onions{2}(finely chopped),
@red bell pepper{1}(in 1/2-inch dice), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced),
@chili powder{1/4%cup}, @ground cumin{1%tbsp}, @ground coriander{2%tsp},
@red pepper flakes{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} and @cayenne pepper{1/2%tsp}.
Cook ~{10%minutes}, stirring now and then, until the vegetables soften and start
to brown.

Turn the heat to medium-high. Add half the @ground beef{2%lb}(85% lean) and cook
~{4%minutes}, breaking it up, until no longer pink. Add the rest and cook
~{4%minutes} more.

Stir in the @kidney beans{2%cans}(15 oz each, drained and rinsed),
@diced tomatoes{28%oz}(with juice), @tomato puree{28%oz} and @salt{1/2%tsp}.
Bring to a boil, then turn to low, cover, and simmer ~{1%hour}, stirring now and
then.

Uncover and simmer ~{1%hour} more, until the beef is tender and the chili is
dark and slightly thick. If it catches on the bottom, stir in a splash of water.

Season with salt and serve with @limes{2}(cut into wedges).

> For a slow cooker, do the first step on the stove, then move everything to the
> cooker and cook on high ~{4%hours}.
